
                    ########################
                    #  ITXC_structure.dat  #
                    ########################

This file lists information on selected structure types.

line 0: separator '************...'
line 1: name of the structure type 
        if alternatives are given, only the first will be used
line 2: space group number, international symbol 
line 3: Schoenflies symbol 
line 4: space group number used to distinguish ALL entries in 
        A. Perlov's symmetry program
line 5: number n of inequivalent site types
following n lines: Wyckoff symbol, coordinates in crystallographic
coordinates, number of equivalent sites of the same type,
point group

         ##############################################
         #  EXTEND THIS FILE ACCORDING TO YOUR NEEDS  #
         ##############################################

For a new structure to be added: find out its space group and
copy the corresponding entry from the file ITXC_spacegroups.dat.
If there is a choice concerning the origin (indicated by ':1' 
and ':2',  take 2, because this choice includes the inversion.
Add the structure type name after the separator line. Remove
all lines for the inequivalent site types that do NOT occur 
for the structure type and reduce in line 5 n according to the
remaining number of site types.

E.g.: Cu3Au has space group 221, that allows 14 different site
types: a to n. Cu3Au has only types a and c. Thus the line specifying 
type b and d to n has to be removed and n reduced from 14 to 2.

